    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343-a1">

                <pb facs="0634" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg538"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Liberian Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Barclay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-03-04"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">208/D</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: I have the honour to
                    advise you that the Liberian Government is despatching to the United States Mr.
                    de la Rue, Financial Adviser, for the purpose of concluding the Loan Agreement
                    between the Liberian Government and the Finance Corporation of New York and to
                    settle other matters which might need adjustment in connection with the
                    Firestone Plantation Agreement. Mr. de la Rue is furnished with certified text
                    of the Loan Agreement as amended.</p>
                <p>I should be pleased if you would advise your Government of the contents of this
                    despatch.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin Barclay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
